WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.354
With Lingui, you write copy inline,

2
00:00:03.354 --> 00:00:05.456
extract it to PO catalogs,

3
00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:07.486
translate them, and compile.

4
00:00:07.886 --> 00:00:10.196
Its macros need no keys,

5
00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:12.599
and its compiled
runtime stays small.

6
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.679
General Translation keeps the
same inline copy and generates

7
00:00:16.679 --> 00:00:17.758
the translations.

8
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.250
Your team writes copy
inline inside a T component,

9
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.329
as with Lingui.

10
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:28.295
Then npx gt translate writes
every catalog before the build,

11
00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:29.710
with no compile step.

12
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.484
Reviewers edit the
results in the Dashboard,

13
00:00:32.484 --> 00:00:35.838
and each run reuses
unchanged translations.

14
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.285
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
